  "instance_name": "racist_joke_structure",
  "label": "Racist Joke Structure: 'What's the Difference?'",
  "description": "The rhetorical question 'what's the difference between the 2?' is a common structure in racist jokes that sets up a false equivalence or a degrading comparison. In this case, it is used to imply that one group (the 'first one') is inferior or incapable, while the other (the 'second') is not — a structure that relies on real-world racial hierarchies and stereotypes to be understood.",
